1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,910
Woman: So, I understand you're interested in restaurant work?

2
00:00:04,910 --> 00:00:09,890
Man: Yes. I've got a bit of experience and I can provide references.

3
00:00:09,890 --> 00:00:12,720
Woman: That's good. I can check all that later.

4
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:16,720
Now, Milo's Restaurants have some vacancies at the moment.

5
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:20,410
They're a really good company to work for. Lots of benefits.

6
00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:21,050
Man: Oh right.

7
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:26,274
Woman: Yes. They've got a very good reputation for looking after staff.

8
00:00:26,274 --> 00:00:29,890
For example, all employees get training - even temporary staff.

9
00:00:29,890 --> 00:00:32,980
Man: Oh really? That's quite unusual, isn't it?

10
00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:34,000
Woman: Certainly is.

11
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,420
Man: And do staff get free uniforms too?

12
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:44,170
Woman: Um... you just need to wear a white T-shirt and black trousers, it says here.

13
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:53,140
So I guess not... But another benefit of working for a big company like this is that you can get a discount at any of their restaurants.

14
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:54,490
Man: Even at weekends?

15
00:00:54,490 --> 00:00:57,280
Woman: No, but you'll be working then anyway.

16
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:59,411
Man: Oh yes. I suppose so.

17
00:00:59,411 --> 00:01:03,560
Most of their restaurants are in the city centre, aren't they

18
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:06,160
So, easy to get to by bus?

19
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:09,680
Woman: Yes. That's right. But if you have to do a late shift

20
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,531
and finish work after midnight,

21
00:01:11,531 --> 00:01:14,640
the company will pay for you to get a taxi home.

22
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:17,970
Man: I probably won't need one. I think I'd use my bike.

23
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:24,940
Woman: OK. Now, they do have some quite specific requirements for the kind of person they're looking for.

24
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:27,200
Milo's is a young, dynamic company

25
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:30,067
and they're really keen on creating a strong team.

26
00:01:30,067 --> 00:01:34,590
It's really important that you can fit in and get on well with everyone.

27
00:01:34,590 --> 00:01:38,690
Man: Yeah. I've got no problem with that. It sounds good, actually.

28
00:01:38,690 --> 00:01:41,899
The last place I worked for was quite demanding too.

29
00:01:41,899 --> 00:01:46,070
We had to make sure we gave a really high level of service.

30
00:01:46,070 --> 00:01:50,299
Woman: That's good to hear because that will be equally important at Milo's.

31
00:01:50,299 --> 00:01:53,400
I know they want people who have an eye for detail.

32
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:57,070
Man: That's fine. I'm very used to working in that kind of environment.

33
00:01:57,070 --> 00:02:01,568
Woman: Perfect. So the only other thing that's required is good communication skills,

34
00:02:01,568 --> 00:02:04,780
so you'll need to have a certificate in English.

35
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:08,010
Man: Sure.

36
00:02:08,010 --> 00:02:12,160
Woman: OK. Let's have a look at the current job vacancies at Milo's

37
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:15,310
The first one is in Wivenhoe Street.

38
00:02:15,310 --> 00:02:16,260
Man: Sorry, where?

39
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:26,490
Woman: Wivenhoe. W. I-V-E-N-H-O-E. It's quite central, just off Cork Street.

40
00:02:26,490 --> 00:02:27,630
Man: Oh right.

41
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:30,300
Woman: They're looking for a breakfast supervisor.

42
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:32,060
Man: That would be OK.

43
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:36,550
Woman: So you're probably familiar with the kind of responsibilities involved.

44
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:39,510
Obviously checking that all the portions are correct,

45
00:02:39,510 --> 00:02:45,430
etc., and then things like checking all the procedures for cleaning the equipment are being followed.

46
00:02:45,430 --> 00:02:47,915
Man: OK. And what about the salary?

47
00:02:47,915 --> 00:02:52,260
In my last job I was getting £9.50 per hour

48
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:55,370
I was hoping to get a bit more than that.

49
00:02:55,370 --> 00:02:59,140
Woman: Well, to begin with, you'd be getting £9.75

50
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:03,820
but that goes up to £11.25 after three months.

51
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:07,810
Man: That's not too bad. And I suppose it's a very early start?

52
00:03:07,810 --> 00:03:11,715
Woman: Mmm. That's the only unattractive thing about this job.

53
00:03:11,715 --> 00:03:14,910
But then you have the afternoons and evenings free.

54
00:03:14,910 --> 00:03:17,900
So the restaurant starts serving breakfast from 7 a.

55
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:23,380
m. And you'd have to be there at 5.30 to set everything up

56
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,540
But you'd be finished at 12.30.

57
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:29,570
Man: Mmm. Well, as you say, there are advantages to that.

58
00:03:29,570 --> 00:03:34,670
Woman: Now, you might also be interested in the job at the City Road branch.

59
00:03:34,670 --> 00:03:38,750
That's for a junior chef, so again a position of responsibility.

60
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:41,070
Man: I might prefer that, actually.

61
00:03:41,070 --> 00:03:47,850
Woman: Right, well obviously this role would involve supporting the sous chef and other senior staff.

62
00:03:47,850 --> 00:03:52,220
And you'd be responsible for making sure there's enough stock each week

63
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:54,500
and sorting out all the deliveries.

64
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:56,320
Man: I've never done that before

65
00:03:56,360 --> 00:04:00,320
but I imagine it's fairly straightforward, once you get the hang of it.

66
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:04,491
Woman: Yes, and you'd be working alongside more experienced staff to begin with,

67
00:04:04,491 --> 00:04:07,470
so I'm sure it wouldn't be a problem.

68
00:04:07,470 --> 00:04:13,250
The salary's slightly higher here. It's an annual salary of £23,000.

69
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:14,220
Man: Right.

70
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:19,054
Woman: I know that if they like you, it's likely you'll be promoted quite quickly.

71
00:04:19,054 --> 00:04:20,760
So that's worth thinking about.

72
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:24,930
Man: Yes. It does sound interesting. What are the hours like?

73
00:04:24,930 --> 00:04:28,940
Woman: The usual, I think. There's a lot of evening and weekend work

74
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:31,180
but they're closed on Mondays.

75
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:34,760
But you do get one Sunday off every four weeks

76
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:37,420
So would you like me to send off your...
